\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces The falsifiable matrix. The sign structure of Sec.~\ref {sec:model} predicts co-drift in $+x$ for the mixed pair, reversal under mirroring, a weaker runaway at wider separation, and \emph  {no} net drift for same-sector pairs and lone stars. Every cell was solved to Ham ${\leq }0.09\%$, Mom ${\leq }0.08\%$ (Appendix~\ref {app:constraints}), verified at $t=0$ against independently computed star fingerprints (all within $0.2\%$), and evolved under identical numerics. Drifts in code units at $t_{\rm  end}$ ($t=40$ for singles, $60$ for pairs).}}{3}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:matrix}{{I}{3}{The falsifiable matrix. The sign structure of Sec.~\ref {sec:model} predicts co-drift in $+x$ for the mixed pair, reversal under mirroring, a weaker runaway at wider separation, and \emph {no} net drift for same-sector pairs and lone stars. Every cell was solved to Ham ${\leq }0.09\%$, Mom ${\leq }0.08\%$ (Appendix~\ref {app:constraints}), verified at $t=0$ against independently computed star fingerprints (all within $0.2\%$), and evolved under identical numerics. Drifts in code units at $t_{\rm end}$ ($t=40$ for singles, $60$ for pairs)}{table.1}{}}
