\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Constraint monitoring for the reference cell \texttt  {pair\_pm} (black) against the single-star controls (light gray; solid canonical, dashed phantom, run to $t=40$): (a)~Hamiltonian constraint $\mathcal  {H}$, composite $L_2$ norms (solid) and the reference cell's $L_\infty $ norm (dash--dotted); (b)~momentum constraint $\mathcal  {M}$, $L_2$ norms. The equal-$|M|$ rerun lies indistinguishably under the black curves and is omitted. The birth spike from the matter repaint relaxes within $t\lesssim 1$ to the truncation floor; the dotted vertical line marks $t=30$, the end of the clean measurement window; the fine AMR level first activates at $t\approx 47.5$, leaving no feature in the norms.}}{8}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:constraints}{{6}{8}{Constraint monitoring for the reference cell \texttt {pair\_pm} (black) against the single-star controls (light gray; solid canonical, dashed phantom, run to $t=40$): (a)~Hamiltonian constraint $\mathcal {H}$, composite $L_2$ norms (solid) and the reference cell's $L_\infty $ norm (dash--dotted); (b)~momentum constraint $\mathcal {M}$, $L_2$ norms. The equal-$|M|$ rerun lies indistinguishably under the black curves and is omitted. The birth spike from the matter repaint relaxes within $t\lesssim 1$ to the truncation floor; the dotted vertical line marks $t=30$, the end of the clean measurement window; the fine AMR level first activates at $t\approx 47.5$, leaving no feature in the norms}{figure.6}{}}
